# Title: Concise Execution Rules for Cursor

- Execute only what is explicitly requested.
- Implement changes directly without adding a summary.
- Do not add unnecessary text explaining what was done in the code.
- Provide explanations only when explicitly asked.
- Avoid repetitions and unnecessary wording.
- Stay concise and organized in all responses.
- Once the implementation is complete, not necessary to explain what was completed
